<!-- SCROLL 02: HOW THE WEEK UNRAVELLED START -->
<section id="scroll-02" aria-labelledby="h2x">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="num rv"><b>02</b> The timeline</p>
    <h2 class="h2 rv d1" id="h2x">How the week <span class="c">unravelled</span></h2>
    <p class="lede rv d2">What was reported, what each organisation said, and what is still unexplained.</p>
    <p class="cue rv d2" id="tlcue">Tap an event to explore</p>
    <ol class="tl" id="tl" aria-describedby="tlcue">
      <li class="spine" aria-hidden="true" style="list-style:none"></li>
      <li class="fill" aria-hidden="true" style="list-style:none"></li>
      <li class="ev">
        <button type="button" class="row" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="p1" id="b1"><span class="date"><b>12</b><i>Nov<br>Thu</i></span><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="t"><b>Microsoft 365</b><span>Global outage of Outlook, Teams and other services</span></span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="pane glass" id="p1" role="region" aria-labelledby="b1" hidden>
          <dl>
            <dt>Disruption</dt><dd><span class="tag t-c">Confirmed</span>A global outage crippled online communications for businesses and governments for <strong>over 24 hours</strong>.</dd>
            <dt>Cause</dt><dd><span class="tag t-o">Company</span>Microsoft blamed <strong>server issues</strong> and said it was not aware of malicious activity. Other reports describe a months-old bug and a cascading networking problem. These may be different layers of the same failure, and the reporting does not reconcile them.</dd>
            <dt>Recovery</dt><dd>Microsoft said on Saturday 14 November that services had fully recovered.</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="ev">
        <button type="button" class="row" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="p2" id="b2"><span class="date"><b>13</b><i>Nov<br>Fri</i></span><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="t"><b>Federal Aviation Administration</b><span>Nearly five-hour national ground stop</span></span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="pane glass" id="p2" role="region" aria-labelledby="b2" hidden>
          <dl>
            <dt>Disruption</dt><dd><span class="tag t-c">Confirmed</span>Airlines cancelled <strong>more than 18,000 flights over three days</strong>. It was the longest such outage since the 11 September 2001 attacks.</dd>
            <dt>Cause</dt><dd><span class="tag t-o">Official</span>Blamed on the installation of <strong>a single router</strong> at a remote facility in Arkansas. Other reports describe a router update.</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="ev">
        <button type="button" class="row" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="p3" id="b3"><span class="date"><b>16</b><i>Nov<br>Mon</i></span><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="t"><b>JPMorgan Chase, and other banks</b><span>Transaction and online-banking problems</span></span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="pane glass" id="p3" role="region" aria-labelledby="b3" hidden>
          <dl>
            <dt>Disruption</dt><dd><span class="tag t-c">Confirmed for Chase</span>Chase had problems processing transactions.</dd>
            <dt>Differing account</dt><dd>Other reports say online access to balances and transfers was disrupted while card payments appeared to keep working, for less than a day. Bank of America and Wells Fargo were also named, without dates or causes.</dd>
            <dt>Cause</dt><dd><span class="tag t-o">Company</span>Chase cited <strong>a software bug</strong> and said there was no evidence it was cyber-related.</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="ev">
        <button type="button" class="row" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="p4" id="b4"><span class="date"><b>16</b><i>Nov<br>Mon</i></span><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="t"><b>United Airlines</b><span>Many departures halted</span></span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="pane glass" id="p4" role="region" aria-labelledby="b4" hidden>
          <dl>
            <dt>Disruption</dt><dd><span class="tag t-c">Confirmed</span>United said a computer problem forced a halt to many departing flights.</dd>
            <dt>Scale</dt><dd>Not quantified. One report described it as a minor disruption.</dd>
            <dt>Cause</dt><dd><strong>Not specified</strong> beyond “a computer problem”.</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="ev">
        <button type="button" class="row" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="p5" id="b5"><span class="date"><b>18</b><i>Nov<br>Wed</i></span><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="t"><b>Apple</b><span>Some services reported down</span></span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="pane glass" id="p5" role="region" aria-labelledby="b5" hidden>
          <dl>
            <dt>Disruption</dt><dd><span class="tag t-c">Reported</span>Apple announced that some of its services were down. iCloud photos are mentioned.</dd>
            <dt>Scale and cause</dt><dd><strong>Not specified</strong> in the reporting.</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="offnote rv"><b>17 Nov · Official response</b>Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin said the outages were not tied to cyberattacks but to ageing computer systems needing upgrades. Secretary of State Marco Rubio separately said every indicator pointed away from hostile actors. These are assessments, not published investigation findings.</div>
    <p class="alsonote rv"><b>Also reported, date not established:</b> the NSA’s confidential telephone network went down. People inside the agency said it had been failing for a year.</p>
  </div>
